# GitHub Actions FTP deploy — required repository secrets
#
# Settings → Secrets and variables → Actions → New repository secret
#
# FTP_SERVER       Hostname, e.g. ftp.zhengkyc.com or ftp.yourhost.com
# FTP_USERNAME     FTP account username
# FTP_PASSWORD     FTP account password
# FTP_SERVER_DIR   Remote app root WITH trailing slash, e.g. /public_html/ispbilling/
#
# Optional:
# FTP_PORT         Default 21 (use 990 for implicit FTPS if your host requires it)
# FTP_PROTOCOL     Default ftps — use "ftp" only if your host does not support TLS
#
# First-time server setup (once, on the host):
# 1. Upload or create .env with production values (never committed; excluded from deploy)
# 2. php artisan key:generate
# 3. php artisan migrate --force
# 4. php artisan storage:link
# 5. Ensure storage/ and bootstrap/cache/ are writable (755 or 775)
#
# After each push to main, GitHub Actions builds vendor + assets and syncs via FTP.
